      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxville%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Scott County, where Oxville sits, was organized in 1839 and covers about 251 square miles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://genealogytrails.com/ill/scott/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The land that became Oxville was originally owned by the Kickapoo Indians before the 1819 treaty of Edwardsville ceded it to the U.S. government.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://genealogytrails.com/ill/scott/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early settlers in the area included Kentuckians such as Thomas Stevens and John Scott, who built the first houses in the county.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://genealogytrails.com/ill/scott/"
    },
    {
